// strategy.example.json — TEMPLATE, not read by the bot.
//
// How to use:
//   1. Copy this file to `strategy.json` in the project root.
//   2. Strip out these `//` comment lines (JSON does not support comments —
//      this template uses them for documentation only; the real
//      strategy.json must be valid JSON).
//   3. Edit an existing profile's `filters`/`section`/`llmEnabled`/
//      `darwinEnabled`/`autoEvolve`, or add a new top-level key with its
//      own profile — then point `strategy` in live-config.json at its name.
//   4. If you skip this step entirely, the bot auto-creates strategy.json
//      with these same 5 built-in profiles on first run.
//
// This is where screener.filters, screener.section, llm.enabled, and
// darwin.enabled/autoEvolve now live (moved out of live-config.json).
// Each profile is fully self-contained — applyStrategy() overwrites those
// fields wholesale from whichever profile `strategy` (in live-config.json)
// points to, on every config build. Everything else (TP/SL/trailing/
// position size/LLM & Darwin tuning) stays in live-config.json and is
// never touched here.
